WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.524
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A two.

2
00:00:05.824 --> 00:00:09.571
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.871 --> 00:00:16.598
Unit sixteen: Used to (past habits). Today you will talk about things you did in the past but not now.

4
00:00:16.898 --> 00:00:19.620
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.567 --> 00:00:23.707
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:25.528
Used to.

7
00:00:26.517 --> 00:00:29.561
Used to means a past habit or state that is finished.

8
00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:31.720
I used to play outside.

9
00:00:32.317 --> 00:00:34.725
Your turn. Say: Used to.

10
00:00:37.567 --> 00:00:38.684
Used to.

11
00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:40.648
Past habit.

12
00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:44.845
Past habit means something you did regularly in the past.

13
00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:47.368
Swimming was a past habit.

14
00:00:47.983 --> 00:00:50.879
Your turn. Say: Past habit.

15
00:00:53.733 --> 00:00:54.955
Past habit.

16
00:00:55.717 --> 00:00:56.753
No longer.

17
00:00:57.750 --> 00:00:59.773
No longer means not any more.

18
00:01:00.383 --> 00:01:01.860
I no longer live there.

19
00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:05.044
Your turn. Say: No longer.

20
00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:09.017
No longer.

21
00:01:09.783 --> 00:01:10.750
Change.

22
00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:14.191
Change means the process of becoming different.

23
00:01:14.783 --> 00:01:16.260
There is a big change.

24
00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:19.200
Your turn. Say: Change.

25
00:01:22.067 --> 00:01:23.056
Change.

26
00:01:23.817 --> 00:01:24.690
Habit.

27
00:01:25.683 --> 00:01:28.519
Habit means something you do again and again.

28
00:01:29.117 --> 00:01:30.617
Reading is a good habit.

29
00:01:31.217 --> 00:01:33.312
Your turn. Say: Habit.

30
00:01:36.167 --> 00:01:36.994
Habit.

31
00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:38.728
Routine.

32
00:01:39.717 --> 00:01:42.332
Routine means your usual way of doing things.

33
00:01:42.917 --> 00:01:44.440
My routine is simple.

34
00:01:45.050 --> 00:01:47.435
Your turn. Say: Routine.

35
00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:51.394
Routine.

36
00:01:52.150 --> 00:01:53.186
Before.

37
00:01:54.183 --> 00:01:56.055
Before means earlier than now.

38
00:01:56.650 --> 00:01:58.139
I lived here before.

39
00:01:58.750 --> 00:02:01.193
Your turn. Say: Before.

40
00:02:04.033 --> 00:02:04.965
Before.

41
00:02:05.717 --> 00:02:06.439
Now.

42
00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:08.950
Now means at this time.

43
00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:11.039
Now I study English.

44
00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:14.175
Your turn. Say: Now.

45
00:02:17.033 --> 00:02:17.918
Now.

46
00:02:18.733 --> 00:02:22.117
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:22.983 --> 00:02:25.389
Visal, what did you use to do as a child?

48
00:02:26.483 --> 00:02:38.554
I used to play outside every day. Used to describes a habit or state in the past that is finished. It shows a change: I don't play outside now.

49
00:02:39.650 --> 00:02:40.767
How do we form it?

50
00:02:41.883 --> 00:02:54.685
Used to + base verb: She used to live in the countryside. For negatives and questions we use didn't use to and did you use to: Did you use to cycle? I didn't use to like fish.

51
00:02:55.783 --> 00:02:57.260
Is it the same as would?

52
00:02:58.350 --> 00:03:10.641
For habits, yes: I would play outside. But for states we only use used to: I used to be shy. Do not confuse with be used to, which means be familiar with.

53
00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:13.347
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:14.183 --> 00:03:17.181
Grammar focus: Used to plus base verb.

55
00:03:17.481 --> 00:03:18.726
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:19.417 --> 00:03:21.811
I used to play outside every day.

57
00:03:22.717 --> 00:03:24.507
She didn't use to like fish.

58
00:03:25.417 --> 00:03:27.439
Did you use to cycle to school?

59
00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:37.313
Used to + base verb describes a finished habit or state. Questions and negatives: did you use to…? / didn't use to. It shows a change from past to now.

60
00:03:38.050 --> 00:03:41.225
Be careful! Don't say: I use to play football.

61
00:03:43.167 --> 00:03:45.004
Say: I used to play football.

62
00:03:45.304 --> 00:03:47.338
Use used to for the past habit.

63
00:03:48.133 --> 00:03:51.099
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:52.948
When I Was Little.

65
00:03:53.248 --> 00:03:56.211
When I was little, I used to play outside every day.

66
00:03:57.200 --> 00:04:00.140
My grandmother used to tell us stories before bed.

67
00:04:01.133 --> 00:04:03.829
I didn't use to like fish, but now I love it.

68
00:04:04.833 --> 00:04:08.435
We no longer live in the village, so that routine has changed.

69
00:04:09.433 --> 00:04:11.166
Did you use to walk to school?

70
00:04:12.267 --> 00:04:16.547
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:17.383 --> 00:04:20.079
I blank play football every day as a child.

72
00:04:20.379 --> 00:04:24.091
A, use to. B, used to. C, using to.

73
00:04:27.633 --> 00:04:29.424
The answer is B: used to.

74
00:04:30.583 --> 00:04:32.327
She didn't blank like fish.

75
00:04:32.627 --> 00:04:36.269
A, used to. B, use to. C, uses to.

76
00:04:39.833 --> 00:04:41.763
The answer is B: use to.

77
00:04:42.917 --> 00:04:44.429
'No longer' means blank.

78
00:04:44.729 --> 00:04:48.870
A, not any more. B, very soon. C, always.

79
00:04:52.433 --> 00:04:54.584
The answer is A: not any more.

80
00:04:55.750 --> 00:04:57.320
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:57.620 --> 00:05:03.073
A, I used to going there.. B, I used to go there.. C, I use to go there..

82
00:05:06.633 --> 00:05:08.912
The answer is B: I used to go there..

83
00:05:10.050 --> 00:05:13.071
According to the reading, what did the grandmother use to do?

84
00:05:13.371 --> 00:05:17.594
A, tell stories. B, cook fish. C, play football.

85
00:05:21.133 --> 00:05:23.470
The answer is A: tell stories.

86
00:05:24.667 --> 00:05:28.271
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:29.117 --> 00:05:31.941
Write a sentence about something you used to do as a child.

88
00:05:40.750 --> 00:05:42.308
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:42.608 --> 00:05:53.762
When I was a child, I used to climb trees with my cousins. We used to come home with dirty clothes. Now I don't climb trees, but I remember those days with joy.

90
00:05:54.062 --> 00:05:55.585
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:56.483 --> 00:06:00.889
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and used to plus base verb.

92
00:06:01.189 --> 00:06:05.002
Today's value is gratitude. Say thank you for your home and family.

93
00:06:05.302 --> 00:06:08.129
See you in Unit seventeen. Goodbye!

94
00:06:08.429 --> 00:06:11.696
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

